{"seq":null,"commit_to":{"owner":"pertson-labs","repo":"e2e-expert-repo","branch":"live/first-version--5c5a81a0d95a"},"doc_stem":"2026-08-23-1-e2e-overwrite-1787476785913","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":7,"spec_hash":"c834f46b2b0c"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-ba19e5f6","payload":{"expand_iris":["ns__Strategy","ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst","ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping"],"focus":"document review, first version, reviewer assignment, versioning","rationale":"The document is a minimal first-version submission with a reviewer assignment (Xena ExpertGH) and no substantive body text. The perspective map surfaced only the Strategy area and its two child decisions (DiagnosticFirst, KnowledgeMapping) as focus-relevant material. I expanded all three to witness depth to give the extraction passes the full organizational context around Xena's engagement methodology, since the document's reviewer assignment and 'first version' note could relate to the diagnostic-first approach. No other areas in the map or index substantively overlapped with this document's content; the document is too sparse to justify reaching into unrelated regions.","n8n_execution_id":"144594","expansion_count":3,"context":"# Perspective — pertson-labs/e2e-expert-repo @ dc4d28e63e1d15ca56f69a40b115a5f8075afcbe\npin: 0a06213034ed1091a23a076ad5a7b5e57073a098\n\nSections, stable-first: (1) THE MAP — the richest areas at steering grain; (2) AREA INDEX — every other area, named, one line each; (3) ACTIVE SURFACE — recent + load-bearing witnesses; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map and index never vary with your focus; your per-call material is at the end.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: document review, first version, reviewer assignment, versioning (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\n### ns__Strategy\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping  (already in your context)\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst, ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping, ^ns__Strategy\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","